    "designMd": "# Design System: Folio3 Parking\n\n## 1. Visual Theme & Atmosphere\nAn orderly, calm internal tool that works like good car-park signage: you read it at a glance, nothing is decorative, and every number means something. The surfaces are a cool concrete neutral with crisp hairline structure, and one deep teal accent marks the thing you can act on right now.\n\n- **Density: 6, \"Daily App Balanced\".** Employee views are roomier and lead with one clear status and one action. Admin and guard views are tighter and run on tables and lists.\n- **Variance: 4, \"Offset Asymmetric\" kept mild.** Layouts sit on a 12-column grid. The main content is left-aligned and a narrower context column sits on the right. Nothing is centred except the sign-in panel.\n- **Motion: 4, \"Fluid CSS\".** Motion is short and functional. State changes never snap. There is one live element at most and one signature moment.\n\nThe mood: clinical but friendly, like a well-lit, freshly painted parking level.\n\n## 2. Color Palette & Roles\nAll neutrals come from one cool slate family. There is no warm or cool gray switching.\n\n- **Canvas Concrete** (#F6F7F7): app background behind all content.\n- **Surface White** (#FFFFFF): panels, tables, forms, sheets.\n- **Sunken Tint** (#EEF1F2): table header rows, row hover, read-only fields, skeleton base.\n- **Asphalt Ink** (#16191C): primary text, headings, the \"Reserved\" status outline. Never pure black.\n- **Kerb Gray** (#5E666E): secondary text, metadata, helper text, the \"Claimed\" status fill.\n- **Hairline Rule** (#DDE1E4): 1px borders, dividers, table rules, input borders.\n- **Bay Teal** (#0F6E66): **the single accent.** Primary buttons, the \"Claimable\" status, active nav item, focus rings, links, the live available-space count.\n- **Bay Teal Wash** (#E3F0EE): the accent at low strength. Selected rows, active tab background, Claimable chip fill.\n- **Signal Red** (#B42318): functional only. Errors, access denied, LPR mismatch, destructive confirms.\n- **Caution Ochre** (#9A5B13): functional only. Warnings such as a plate not on file or a pending verification.\n\nRules:\n- Teal is the only colour that invites action.\n- Red and ochre are status signals only. They are never decoration and never button fills, except a destructive confirm.\n- No gradients, glows or neon. No purple or blue \"AI\" hues.\n\n## 3. Typography Rules\n- **Display / Headlines: Hanken Grotesk.** Weights 600–700. Tracking −0.02em at 24px and above, −0.03em at 40px and above. Hierarchy comes from weight and colour, not huge sizes. Scale: 32 / 24 / 20 / 16px. Page titles use `clamp(1.5rem, 1.2rem + 1vw, 2rem)`.\n- **Body: Public Sans.** 15–16px at 1.55 leading. Prose capped at 65ch. Table text 14px at 1.4.\n- **Mono: IBM Plex Mono.** Used for licence plates, space IDs, floor codes, timestamps, audit-log entries and every count or number in tables.\n- **Numerals:** `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` on all counts, dates and report figures.\n- **Labels:** small uppercase labels (11–12px, weight 600) get +0.08em tracking in Kerb Gray.\n- **Punctuation:** curly quotes, en dashes for ranges (Mon–Fri, 08:00–18:00), a real ellipsis.\n- **Dates:** formatted for the locale (\"Tue, 14 Oct\").\n- **Typographic contrast:** one per page, through case. Uppercase mono for identifiers against sentence-case sans for everything else.\n- **Banned:** Inter, Roboto, Montserrat, DM Sans, Plus Jakarta Sans, Space Grotesk, Manrope and Sora. No serif anywhere, because this is software UI.\n\n## 4. Component Stylings\n- **Buttons**\n  - Height 40px, with a 44px tap area on touch screens. Soft 6px radius.\n  - Primary: Bay Teal fill with white text. Secondary: white with a Hairline Rule border and Asphalt Ink text. Destructive: Signal Red only inside confirm dialogs.\n  - Press: `scale(0.97)` at 90ms. Hover darkens the fill to #0B5A53. A trailing arrow icon nudges 3px.\n  - Labels are product verbs (\"Claim a space\", \"Release today\", \"Record entry\"), never \"Get started\" or \"Submit\".\n  - No glows and no pulsing.\n- **Status chips (Reserved / Claimable / Claimed)**\n  - 24px tall, 4px radius, uppercase mono label at 11px with +0.08em tracking.\n  - Reserved: Asphalt Ink 1px outline. Claimable: Bay Teal Wash fill with Bay Teal text. Claimed: Kerb Gray fill with white text.\n  - Each status is shown in words, never by colour alone.\n- **Bay Plate identifier**\n  - Licence plates and assigned space/floor are set in IBM Plex Mono uppercase inside a white box: 1px Asphalt Ink border, 4px radius, 2px Bay Teal left rule like a painted bay line.\n  - The large version (40px) is used for the assigned space. The inline version (14px) is used in tables.\n- **Cards / Panels**\n  - White surface, 1px Hairline Rule border, 8px radius, no shadow by default.\n  - A panel is used only to group one status and its action.\n  - Admin lists are not cards. They are tables on the canvas, with hairline row dividers and a Sunken Tint header.\n- **Tables**\n  - 44px rows, sticky header, sortable column headers with a small caret. Numbers are right-aligned and tabular.\n  - Row hover is Sunken Tint. The selected row is Bay Teal Wash with a 2px teal left rule.\n  - Row actions sit at the far right as text buttons, not icon clusters.\n- **Inputs / Forms**\n  - Label above (13px, weight 600). Input 40px tall with a 1px Hairline Rule border and 6px radius.\n  - Helper text below in Kerb Gray. Error text below in Signal Red with the border switched to red.\n  - Focus: 2px Bay Teal outline at 2px offset. No floating labels.\n  - Plate inputs are mono uppercase.\n- **Navigation**\n  - Admin uses a left rail, 232px wide, with text labels and minimal icons. The active item has a Bay Teal Wash background and a teal left rule.\n  - Employee and guard views use a slim top bar with the user menu.\n  - On mobile the rail collapses to a bottom sheet menu.\n- **Dialogs / Sheets:** white, 8px radius, a single-level shadow, a 40% Asphalt Ink backdrop, and a focus trap.\n- **Loaders:** skeleton blocks in Sunken Tint matching the exact row and panel dimensions, with a gentle shimmer only while loading. No spinners.\n- **Empty states:** one plain sentence saying what is missing, plus the specific action to fill it, set on the canvas with a hairline outline drawing of a parking bay. No illustrations of people.\n- **Error states:** inline beside the cause, in Signal Red text with a short explanation, a retry action and a contact path where access is blocked.\n\n## 5. Layout Principles\n- **Grid:** 12 columns, max-width 1320px, 24px gutters, 32px outer padding on desktop.\n- **Employee views:** the main status/action block spans columns 1–7 and supporting detail (history, vehicles) spans columns 8–12.\n- **Admin views:** a full-width table area beside the left rail. Filters sit in one row above the table, not in a sidebar.\n- **Guard console:** the densest layout. The current verification spans columns 1–8 at large size and the recent-entries list spans columns 9–12.\n- **Sign-in:** a single narrow panel, 400px, placed at column 2 rather than dead centre, with a plain product name above it.\n- Spacing scale is 4 / 8 / 12 / 16 / 24 / 32 / 48px, and section gaps use `clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem)`.\n- No overlapping elements and no absolute-positioned stacking. Use CSS Grid, not `calc()` percentage hacks.\n- Full-height layouts use `min-h-[100dvh]`.\n- **Responsive:**\n  - Below 768px everything collapses to one column and tables become stacked row lists with the identifier first.\n  - Touch targets are at least 44px and body text at least 16px.\n  - No horizontal scroll, except inside a table wrapper that is explicitly marked as scrollable.\n\n## 6. Motion & Interaction\nMotion confirms state. It never decorates.\n- Transitions use transform and opacity only.\n- Entering motion uses an ease-out curve and exits are about 30% faster.\n- Status chip changes cross-fade in 160ms.\n- Lists insert with a fade and an 8px shift.\n- Spring feel (stiffness 100, damping 20) is used only for the signature moment.\n\nFull tokens are in §9.\n\n## 7. Anti-Patterns (Banned)\n- No emojis.\n- No Inter or other AI-default fonts. No serif fonts.\n- No pure black (#000000).\n- No neon, outer glows, gradients, blobs or glassmorphism.\n- No 3-equal-card rows and no bento tiles.\n- No KPI card rows with sparklines and green \"+12%\".\n- No icon-in-rounded-square feature cards. No sparkle icons.\n- No pill \"New\" badges.\n- No generic names (\"John Doe\", \"Acme\"). Use realistic Folio3-style names and plates.\n- No fake round numbers.\n- No AI clichés (\"Seamless\", \"Elevate\", \"Unleash\").\n- No \"Scroll to explore\", chevrons or bouncing arrows.\n- No custom cursors.\n- No pulsing CTA buttons.\n- No typewriter text.\n- No identical fade-up on every section.\n- No more than one perpetual animation per screen.\n- No broken image links. Use SVG avatars with initials.\n\n## 8. Voice & Font Rationale\n- **Voice:** orderly, civic, quick.\n- **Display: Hanken Grotesk.** Its compact, slightly squared grotesk forms read like wayfinding signage, which suits a tool people glance at in a lobby or at a barrier. Google Fonts.\n- **Body: Public Sans.** It is a neutral, highly legible civic face built for government-style forms, which fits a calm internal utility full of forms and tables. Google Fonts.\n- **Mono: IBM Plex Mono.** Its clear zero/O and 1/I distinction matters for licence plates and space IDs. Google Fonts.\n\n## 9. Motion System\n- **Tokens:**\n  - Durations: instant 90ms, quick 160ms, base 260ms, slow 420ms, scene 700ms.\n  - Easings: ease-out `cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1)`, ease-in `cubic-bezier(0.7,0,0.84,0)`, ease-inout `cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)`, plus a spring `linear()` curve.\n  - Travel: 8–12px.\n- **Entrance:** on page load, the page title, then the primary status block, then the supporting column rise 12px with fade. 60ms stagger, under 700ms total. Tables reveal as one group.\n- **Scroll-linked:** used only for report charts. Bars grow to their value once as they enter (`animation-timeline: view()`, range entry 0%–40%). No generic section fades.\n- **Interaction feedback:**\n  - Buttons: press scale 0.97, arrow nudges 3px on hover.\n  - Table rows: tint to Sunken Tint in 160ms.\n  - Links: underline draws from the left.\n  - Inputs: focus ring fades in over 90ms.\n- **State transitions:**\n  - The tab indicator slides between tabs over 260ms.\n  - Accordions and filter panels open with `grid-template-rows: 0fr → 1fr`.\n  - Rows insert or remove with a 160ms fade and 8px shift.\n  - Dialogs and sheets enter over 420ms with ease-out.\n  - Detail pages use the View Transitions API on the shared name/plate element where supported.\n- **Ambient (max 1):** a live dot beside the real-time available-space count or the guard's live LPR feed. Opacity breathes 1 → 0.6 on an 8s cycle. Nothing else loops.\n- **Signature moment, \"Bay Assigned\":** when a space is claimed or an entry is recorded, the Bay Plate identifier unmasks bottom-to-top (`clip-path`) and its digits roll up to the real value over 600ms with the spring easing, in tabular figures.\n- **Reduced motion:** under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`, entrances become instant, chart growth and the live dot are removed, and state changes keep at most a 120ms fade. Content is never hidden waiting for an animation.\n\n```css\n:root{\n  --dur-instant:90ms;--dur-quick:160ms;--dur-base:260ms;--dur-slow:420ms;--dur-scene:700ms;\n  --ease-out:cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1);--ease-in:cubic-bezier(0.7,0,0.84,0);\n  --ease-inout:cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1);\n  --ease-spring:linear(0,0.009,0.035 2.1%,0.141,0.281 6.7%,0.723 12.9%,0.938 16.7%,1.017,1.077 21.4%,1.121 24%,1.149 27%,1.159,1.154 33%,1.051 43.2%,1.013 49.5%,0.996 57%,1.001 72%,1);\n  --accent:#0F6E66;--canvas:#F6F7F7;--ink:#16191C;--rule:#DDE1E4;\n}\n@keyframes rise{from{opacity:0;transform:translateY(12px)}to{opacity:1;transform:none}}\n@keyframes unmask{from{clip-path:inset(100% 0 0 0)}to{clip-path:inset(0)}}\n@keyframes roll{from{transform:translateY(0.6em);opacity:0}to{transform:none;opacity:1}}\n@keyframes breathe{0%,100%{opacity:1}50%{opacity:.6}}\n@keyframes grow{from{transform:scaleY(0)}to{transform:scaleY(1)}}\n.enter{animation:rise var(--dur-scene) var(--ease-out) both}\n.bay-plate.assigned{animation:unmask 600ms var(--ease-spring) both}\n.bay-plate.assigned .digit{animation:roll 600ms var(--ease-spring) both}\n.live-dot{animation:breathe 8s var(--ease-inout) infinite}\n.btn:active{transform:scale(.97);transition:transform var(--dur-instant) var(--ease-out)}\n.chart-bar{transform-origin:bottom;animation:grow linear both;animation-timeline:view();animation-range:entry 0% entry 40%}\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){\n  *{animation:none!important;transition:opacity 120ms linear!important}\n}\n```\n\n## 10. Component Substitutions\n- **KPI card rows with sparklines** → one headline figure with context (e.g. \"37 of 120 spaces free, Floor B2 fullest\"), then a dense sortable table.\n- **Feature/icon cards** → plain labelled panels holding one status and one action.\n- **Sparkle \"AI\" icons** → none. The LPR check is labelled by what it does (\"Plate match\").\n- **Generic \"Get started\" / \"Submit\" CTAs** → product verbs.\n- **Glass or gradient backgrounds** → flat Canvas Concrete with hairline rules.\n- **Icons on every nav link** → text-first navigation, with icons only where they speed recognition.\n- **Mega footer** → none. Version and support contact sit in one mono line in the rail.\n- **Default shadcn look** → 6/8px soft radius family and a teal 2px offset focus ring.\n\n## 11. Human Fingerprint\n- **Unexpected decision: the Bay Plate.** Every space ID, floor code and licence plate is set as a stencilled mono identifier with a painted teal bay-line rule on its left edge. It ties the interface to the physical car park, so a guard and an employee recognise the same object everywhere.\n- **Radius family:** soft. Chips 4px, buttons and inputs 6px, panels and dialogs 8px. Nested inner radius = outer radius − padding.\n- **Elevation:** two levels only. Level 0 is a flat hairline border. Level 1 is dialogs and sheets at `0 8px 24px rgba(22,25,28,0.10)`.\n- **Grid:** 12 columns, 1320px max, 24px gutters. Employee main content spans columns 1–7 and the guard console's main area spans columns 1–8.\n- **Image treatment:** no stock photography. Avatars are SVG initials on Sunken Tint. Empty states use a single-weight 1.5px line drawing of a parking bay in Hairline Rule gray.\n- **Icon set:** Lucide at 1.75 stroke, sized 16px inline and 20px in nav, coloured Kerb Gray or Asphalt Ink, never teal unless active.\n",
